00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.420
Yeah. Or, like, shake things or something.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:45.600
But they didn't do that.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:51.100
They didn't. Or, like, couldn't, couldn't, I mean, isn't Wolverine's whole thing, he, like, regenerates?

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.800
Couldn't he just, like, slowly regain health or something?

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.720
Right. I think that just gave him more health.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.260
Yeah. Yeah, but I like your idea, Joe.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.220
Just, because, yeah, he is immortal.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:00.840
In that sense.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.760
But, I mean, right, right.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:06.720
But, yeah, I actually didn't know about, what is it, Nightcrawler?

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.120
I didn't even know about his special power.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:16.240
I mean, I did try to play as everybody, but, you know, I must have just not realized that I could walk through walls when I played as him.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.680
I don't think I played as him for very long.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.480
You were just respecting the boundaries.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:22.060
Right. I was like, I know what the developers wanted here.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.140
I don't want to glitch.

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:26.600
Well, yeah, that's exactly what it looks like, too, though, Joe.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.580
It's not, it doesn't have a cool effect.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.980
You just walk through the environment.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:39.300
No. It doesn't, it's just to pretend the idea of teleportation because they couldn't figure out how to let a character teleport in this game.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.980
Cyclops, Storm, and Iceman are the projectile people.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:50.340
However, Cyclops is the weakest of the batch because he can only do projectile combat.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.280
Storm and Iceman get the ability to fly, and I get it.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:17:00.440
Like, Iceman must be, like, flying via the snow that he's generating and riding, like, an avalanche or something.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.540
Yeah. But Storm, I don't know.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.560
Like, you know, that makes sense for her, for sure, to fly.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:11.580
And also she shoots, like, lightning bolts instead of the laser beams that Cyclops shoots out.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:17.740
And then. It kind of just looks like fire, but I, I mean, they describe it as lightning, so I'll take that.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:18.580
Right, we're being nice.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:24.480
Yeah. And that's, that's how these characters feel.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:42.320
And, you know, Joe, you were saying, like, you know, the stats might be different and everything, but I don't know if it's just the amount of enemies in this game or whatever, but it didn't feel like the difference between Wolverine and Colossus meant anything through my, you know, a bit limited playtesting with them.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.940
Yeah, I mean, I, I agree.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:49.880
I mean, I think that, I believe that the stats are different because they say they are.

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:53.400
I don't believe it because I experienced any difference.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:58.220
Like, like, I think that you all, like, you get, you get, you pick up health so frequently.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.840
There are just so many enemies.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.480
You kill them really pretty easily as anyone that you are.

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:08.460
Apparently there are some speed differences, but you never really need to move that fast or anything.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:18.540
I mean, there's a couple of times you got to, like, get through a sliding door quickly or something, but, like, I don't know if, like, your speed stat really contributes too much to that, like, one step you need to do.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:30.060
Um, so, yeah, like, I'm sure that there is, like, some damage calculation happening where it's, like, your projectile is more powerful, but, like, most enemies die in, like, one or two hits anyways.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.460
So, I don't know.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.780
I, I, I never really felt the difference between anything.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:46.940
Yeah, I also, um, there's a, there are, so there's speed, strength, uh, I forget what the other two are, but one of them is willpower.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.740
Power, endurance, speed, and willpower.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.560
Yeah, I don't know what willpower is supposed to signify.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:59.680
Um, it, if it has to do with, like, maybe you take less damage, then, I don't know, maybe just give that person more HP.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.980
I, I don't know, like, I, did you guys, do you guys know what willpower is?

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.000
I should, but I don't.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.280
I mean, I remember actually making a mental note of, like, I gotta look that up.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:15.200
Um, I did read through, I mean, admittedly, I wasn't, like, super thorough in reading the manual, but I don't remember seeing it even in the manual.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:17.220
I think they just listed them.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.700
These are the four things.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:24.760
Right, that's what I was gonna say, Sean, is, like, I'm, I'm not sold that, because, yeah, you're right, Joe, they're not listed in the manual.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:30.980
I, you know, I went back and even checked, like, game FAQs to see if, like, the guide on there says, like, what these hidden stats could mean.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.600
It's not even mentioned at all.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:43.780
Um, so I wonder if this is, like, one of those marvel.com things where, uh, people get really upset about this, where they give, like, a power scale to every Marvel character that's ever existed.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:54.560
And when you're ranking, like, 2,000 characters, you're bound to just have, like, erroneous eras, where it's, like, uh, you know, Spider-Man's power is a 7 and Hulk's is a 9.

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.400
It's, like, Spider-Man would get lit up by Hulk.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.620
Like, two power points isn't even, like, that big of a difference.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.540
And those are made up. I'm just saying, like, there's many examples of stuff like that.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:15.280
I wonder if this is just for creative flair of, like, what their stats could be, uh, based on, like, you know, the, to give them some building without actually building it out into the gameplay.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:19.760
I will state that I did feel a difference with speed.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:25.320
So at least speed, I feel that is a real thing, uh, those differences.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:31.520
But, yeah, the one that, the willpower, I don't even know what it means, so I don't know how to prove that.

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:32.720
Some players just give up.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.380
If they have low willpower, then the AI computer just stops.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:37.680
It describes you.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:38.920
Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:02.760
It's two players, always, because the X-Men are always a team, right?

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:04.860
Uh, you can't just be one X-Men.

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:06.420
It's not the Wolverine game.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.480
Uh, we'll play that one.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:12.280
Well, I think that they, I think that they also don't know how to, like, singularize X-Men.

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:13.660
So I just always make sure there's two players on screen.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:17.080
They just dodged that conversation. They didn't want to ask, they didn't want to ask Stan Lee at the time.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.860
They were like, can we say X-Men?

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:19.860
Like, probably not.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:40.020
No, no, no, no. But it brings up a good point of, like, you know, when you have a team idea, in modern games, there would be, like, some kind of, like, puzzle solving of, like, you know, teaming up these two characters means that the gameplay is going to play different than if you were Storm and Nightcrawler, right?

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:46.860
But instead, it's just kind of, like, you're tied down to this AI player if you don't have a friend.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.720
Or, you know, you're tied down to your friend's choice, too.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:56.080
But the AI one has the ability to, like, get stuck and just end the game for you.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.540
Basically softlock itself where it can't figure out how to move around the wall.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:08.720
And that's, like, a, that's just a huge problem that, like, you know, in my experience of playing this game,

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:13.600
I ran into it in my first 15 minutes, so I can't imagine playtesters didn't notice that this could happen.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:21.060
And so you have to play, like, with Nightcrawler to really guarantee that that won't happen because at least he can teleport through the walls.

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:23.280
Oh, you know what?

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:24.560
I didn't even think of that.

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:32.800
But, yeah, it seems like whatever they did with this AI model, like, it is, it's just way too rudimentary.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:42.240
And maybe if every screen was just a, like, a field of enemies with no obstacles, like, maybe it would work then.

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:52.960
Even though I've seen the AI completely glitch out and just start walking back and forth, shooting projectiles over and over.

00:22:53.060 --> 00:22:56.300
Like, many times. Like, within the first 30 seconds of playing.

00:22:57.980 --> 00:22:59.720
Maybe it would happen less.

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:04.080
But they, you know, they didn't want it to be a complete bore.

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:07.220
So they made you have to walk around things.

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.260
But their AI does not know how to do that.

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.800
But, yeah, I guess Nightcrawler fixes that.

00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:19.700
Yeah, I mean, I was initially kind of, like, before I played it, when I just kind of saw what was going to happen, a little impressed.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:25.500
Because I couldn't remember, like, what other games have we played in the NES that had an AI companion?

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.040
No, I can't think of one.

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:34.140
Have we? Yeah, I feel like that was, like, I was, like, surprised that that was, that that was happening, you know, that was doable.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:37.340
Then it made sense once I booted it up and it just doesn't work.

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:41.500
But at first I was like, wow, that's pretty ambitious for the NES.

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:46.760
And I don't know really anything about coding video games and stuff.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:52.960
But I know that, like, for enemies, it's usually a, like, a heat-seeking missile kind of thing.

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:56.380
Where it knows your placement and just the enemies behave a little bit randomly.

00:23:56.380 --> 00:24:00.740
But they also know where you are and try to, like, shoot at you or move towards you.

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:03.760
In this game, you can see that happening.

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:11.000
But because, like, walls are in the way, it's kind of funny that sometimes even enemies will act, like, really stupid.

00:24:11.120 --> 00:24:16.740
And just, like, hug the side of a wall thinking that they're shooting their projectiles at you.

00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:21.660
But they just constantly repeat them into a wall at Infidium until you come to them.

00:24:21.660 --> 00:24:23.640
But the AI does that too.

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:35.380
So really it's like you're tagging along with, um, it's like a rescue mission thing, you know, where you just have to, like, hope that, uh, your AI character survives alongside you.

00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:37.100
I don't think you're penalized if they die, though.

00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:38.600
Like, you can just play on without them.

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:42.040
But, uh, that's hoping that they die and don't get stuck.

00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:49.480
If you can kill one type of enemy, you can kill them all.

00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:52.680
There's, there's different sprites for enemies.

00:24:53.120 --> 00:25:00.300
But the idea is just attack the enemy and, or shoot the projectile at the enemy and then it dies.

00:25:00.720 --> 00:25:02.940
Nothing behaves differently in this game.

00:25:03.120 --> 00:25:10.080
It's just kind of like a smorgasbord of ideas of not even things that I recognize from the comics or anything.

00:25:10.620 --> 00:25:16.620
I'm not really sure, you know, you could, you could complain about the constantly respawning enemies.

00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:18.600
You could complain about the designs of the enemies.

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:26.900
I think the most boring thing is just that the behavior of the enemies and how you just have to kind of, like, deal with them is the worst part of this game.

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:30.000
If they were, if they were fun to fight, that, that'd be a different story.

00:25:31.340 --> 00:25:38.940
I'd say, yeah, the only difference, like, there are different sprites and those different sprites move slightly differently.

00:25:38.940 --> 00:25:42.020
And then you've got some that are different shapes.

00:25:42.280 --> 00:25:46.600
Like, you've got little snakes that run around, but only their head is a hitbox, I think.

00:25:46.800 --> 00:25:55.960
So, uh, they may as well just be, uh, um, uh, just be another, like, single square wide thing.

00:25:55.960 --> 00:26:08.740
Um, and I guess, like, yeah, I mean, it's not like, it's all just, like, palette swapped, but there really isn't any difference in terms of their strength or, uh, how hard they are to kill.

00:26:08.940 --> 00:26:10.460
It's, it's pretty boring.

00:26:11.160 --> 00:26:23.400
And I don't know if that comes down to just the repetitiveness of, it doesn't matter, like, really which X-Men you are, because, you know, because you can only either shoot your projectile or, or hit them.

00:26:23.780 --> 00:26:38.800
I don't know if that's what makes it boring, but I'm thinking about this game as, like, something where it doesn't really matter, like, what you're, you might as well just dodge everything and keep moving forward, uh, to get to the boss.

00:26:38.800 --> 00:26:41.640
Because these enemies, they're just, like, in your way.

00:26:41.780 --> 00:26:44.720
They're not really, like, causing much harm, right?

00:26:45.740 --> 00:26:49.280
Yeah. Well, it's, it's not even, for me, it's not even, like, moving forward.

00:26:49.520 --> 00:26:51.580
Like, the moving forward part, even.

00:26:51.700 --> 00:26:57.860
Like, I, I kind of started doing what you're saying, is, like, I kind of stopped paying too much attention to the enemy unless they were in my way.

00:26:58.100 --> 00:27:00.800
Or I needed health, which was an easy way to just get more health.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:03.960
But moving forward is even, like, not super clear.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:08.680
Like, I feel like there's this aimlessness to the, to the, to the whole game as a whole.

00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:09.640
Like, in general.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:11.020
Where I'm like, oh, I don't know.

00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:12.200
I mean, I guess I could go this way.

00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:13.880
And, like, no, you can't. But there's no wall there.

00:27:13.960 --> 00:27:16.320
You can't go there. There's a wall here, but you can go through that one.

00:27:16.620 --> 00:27:18.640
Like, or, you know, you can go past this part.

00:27:18.780 --> 00:27:19.820
Like, I'm just like, I don't.

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:23.240
It's not, it doesn't feel like a dungeon or a puzzle or a maze.

00:27:23.300 --> 00:27:24.980
It just feels like a mess.

00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:29.100
Yeah, I wasn't sure for most of this game where I was supposed to go.

00:27:29.700 --> 00:27:35.140
And so then I thought, okay, maybe it's a, like, you have to kill a certain amount of enemies.

00:27:35.140 --> 00:27:38.600
And it's sort of like a, like, it's a clear of the stage.

00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:41.000
And then I ended up just doing that for a while.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:51.200
And then I ended up stepping on a, some kind of sprite that was supposed to be some kind of entrance or something.

00:27:51.660 --> 00:27:53.400
And I went somewhere else.

00:27:53.520 --> 00:27:55.060
I'm like, oh, okay, maybe I'm making progress.

00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:58.780
And then I did that for a while and didn't know where the hell I was.

00:27:59.460 --> 00:28:01.300
I eventually made it to a boss.

00:28:02.900 --> 00:28:04.820
But I didn't know how I got there.

00:28:04.960 --> 00:28:06.080
I didn't know how to get back.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:09.440
Yeah, well, that's the other thing.

00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:14.460
I mean, in the manual, it gives you your objective, which is, like, get to the boss, beat the boss, whatever, and then get out.

00:28:14.960 --> 00:28:18.760
But, like, getting, even the beginning of the stage is just, like, you just get to a spot.

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:20.260
And it's like, all right, you won.

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:22.220
And it's not even, like, a door you have to get out.

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:23.220
You're just like, oh, that's the spot.

00:28:23.320 --> 00:28:24.840
There's nothing marking it or anything.

00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:28.080
Like, I guess you have to remember exactly the spot you started in.

00:28:28.180 --> 00:28:29.200
But, like, they're big stages.

00:28:29.200 --> 00:28:31.740
So it's like, just the whole thing feels aimless.

00:28:32.460 --> 00:28:36.920
I'm thinking about another team-based game we had, Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:44.240
And not that we were, like, fond of that game or, you know, maybe we weren't as harsh as people might have expected us to be.

00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:51.100
But that game kind of made the Turtles feel at least a little bit different with the way that their weapons were.

00:28:51.280 --> 00:28:57.020
And you live-swapped them as opposed to, like, being forced to, like, drag Donatello through the stage.

00:28:57.020 --> 00:29:01.340
You could just choose to be like, now I'm going to be Donatello or now I'm going to be Raphael.

00:29:01.340 --> 00:29:07.860
And mostly that was just to manage your health and make sure you, like, you know, continued on.

00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:18.860
But, you know, that's a game where, too, there's, like, the idea of just going across level to level and finding the end point.

00:29:18.940 --> 00:29:21.140
But it didn't feel as obtuse as this.

00:29:21.140 --> 00:29:29.760
And I don't know if that's because that game was a side-scrolling platformer where things were maybe laid out a little clearer or more what we're used to in this top-down thing.

00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:33.600
Specifically in, like, that space level.

00:29:33.800 --> 00:29:35.140
I don't even know if it's space or not.

00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:45.520
But I think the difference between this game and that game, like, despite the most obvious things of, like, you know, it's a side-scroller.

00:29:45.520 --> 00:29:47.360
Things are a little bit more clear with that.

00:29:47.680 --> 00:29:56.600
And it was less of a hassle that you didn't have to deal with a dumbass AI companion.

00:29:57.120 --> 00:30:07.260
I think what was different with Ninja Turtles was it had an idea of visual language.

00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:17.460
And you kind of knew, like, what was a hazard, where you were supposed to go, what was walkable and what wasn't.

00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:24.600
Right. This space level that I was talking about, I guess, like, a ship that you're on, it's very unclear, like, what's walkable.

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:27.760
Because some things are, like, transparent, other things.

00:30:27.940 --> 00:30:31.280
Yeah, like, even what's a door and what's not is weird in this one.

00:30:31.280 --> 00:30:37.380
Because there's, like, blue circles and red circles and squares and, like, those things are the doors.

00:30:37.380 --> 00:30:44.240
I'm like, what? This is almost like a, like a, not an MC Escher.

00:30:45.580 --> 00:30:56.320
It feels like a collage of, like, mismatched patterns that, like, it has an idea of, oh, this one's always going to be the floor.

00:30:56.320 --> 00:30:57.740
And this one's always going to be the wall.

00:30:57.920 --> 00:31:06.540
But, like, either the, whatever the difference is in the actual programming of the game of, like, oh, this is, like, the nav mesh.

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:08.720
And this is the art for it.

00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:10.520
Like, they were misaligned or something.

00:31:11.080 --> 00:31:17.440
What it feels like to me, to be honest, is that, like, you have glitched out of a, like, 2D, you know, like a game like this.

00:31:17.440 --> 00:31:23.040
But, like, you know, and you glitch out of, like, a Final Fantasy game or, like, a Pokemon game or you get, like, a glitch city or something.

00:31:23.080 --> 00:31:27.800
And it's just like, oh, the textures and tiles are all over the place that, like, exist in the code.

00:31:28.120 --> 00:31:30.460
But they were not placed here by humans.

00:31:31.380 --> 00:31:52.200
Yeah. According to the back of the box, and I read this, it's up to you to defeat Magneto.

00:31:52.760 --> 00:31:55.580
But, of course, that's if you can ever find him.

00:31:55.580 --> 00:32:04.440
The game only gives you the five stages, and it's not as simple as beating all five stages like you would in, say, Mega Man.

00:32:04.620 --> 00:32:05.900
And then, you know, Dr.

00:32:05.980 --> 00:32:07.080
Wily reveals himself.

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:09.460
Now Dr. Magneto reveals himself.

00:32:09.940 --> 00:32:11.400
That's not what happens here.

00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:21.200
Instead, you're supposed to put together that at the end of each of these stages, the, like, congratulations thing that you've, um, that you receive at the end of each stage

00:32:21.200 --> 00:32:29.480
is giving you, like, bits and pieces of a code that when you put those code words together across the five levels,

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:37.320
you would then realize, like, oh, I need to look at the box of my game.

