You know what? I like this more. You have to push select, and then you go to the cartridge label, and it just says in the bottom right over by where all the copyright info is,

00:38:18.020 --> 00:38:24.480
it says plus B plus up together on start.

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:26.700
I kind of like this, actually.

00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:27.960
No, this is so stupid.

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:31.000
I remember seeing the red text.

00:38:31.280 --> 00:38:38.360
I kind of like it in the sense that it's, you would think like, okay, there's something weirder.

00:38:38.440 --> 00:38:41.280
Because I did think that. I also remember noticing that able is spelled wrong.

00:38:41.420 --> 00:38:42.280
Yes, able is spelled wrong.

00:38:42.300 --> 00:38:43.460
Because it's trying to make label.

00:38:44.160 --> 00:38:49.020
I still don't know if I understand why contextually the X-Men are solving this puzzle.

00:38:49.120 --> 00:38:50.900
Yeah, like, is there a Riddler equivalent?

00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:52.040
That's what bothers me.

00:38:52.340 --> 00:39:00.240
But, like, it's not as ridiculous of an idea that someone would figure this out as I had thought.

00:39:00.240 --> 00:39:07.100
They should have made it so that you put a magnet up against your television, and that certain image quality screens would change,

00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:09.520
