00:40:21.360 --> 00:40:22.440
I don't like that either.

00:40:22.440 --> 00:40:30.060
No, but I'm saying, like, so think about it, you could beat the level and the text would either be all white or it would be, like, oh, because you killed 30 special enemies.

00:40:30.300 --> 00:40:37.560
Something that is, like, you know, in Super Mario Bros., when you land on an even number, that many number of fireworks happen, right?

00:40:37.620 --> 00:40:39.940
Like, that's something fun and cute and happens right there.

00:40:40.060 --> 00:40:41.020
The payoff is over.

00:40:41.360 --> 00:40:46.480
This is something where it's, like, well, they never told me, like, in the manual, like, make sure you kill 30 special enemies or anything.

00:40:46.480 --> 00:40:49.460
Or even explained why I was getting red text this time.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:55.960
But then you also have to, like, because these levels aren't in a particular order or whatever, like, because you get to choose.

00:40:56.220 --> 00:41:04.300
What if you get them in, like, a different order and then you have to, like, now think about which order they come in to understand the hidden message?

